WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
I want to be in the loop before you email my mother in law.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.480
And what are you here to learn at AI?

3
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:11.280
I'm here to learn about observability and deterministic models,

4
00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:15.360
just to see how to make the results of AI more trusting.

5
00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.920
And even with a proper enterprise scale adoption of AI,

6
00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.320
how do you make sure that the models are not like still hallucinating?

7
00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:26.480
Or if they are like the eval metrics are catching that

8
00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:29.720
and we're able to determine what's actually going on under the hood.

9
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:30.360
Yeah.

10
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:33.400
So we're now in a place where there's so much value, so much data

11
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:37.520
going through our AI, our harnesses that we're going to need to figure out

12
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:38.680
how do we control these things?

13
00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:42.640
Yeah, I think that's probably next is yes, I've got 20 loops going but okay,

14
00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:43.680
what next?

15
00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:46.320
I always ask this question would you trust an agent

16
00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:49.040
to send an email on your behalf right now, sight unseen?

17
00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:52.120
What I do, actually, this is a very valid question

18
00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:55.760
because I've just literally just built a nice little app called Simon EA

19
00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.760
and it can read all my emails and things like that.

20
00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:01.160
But what I get it to do is I get it to only write emails and leave them in draft.

21
00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:04.160
It doesn't have the send ability, so I validate every single thing

22
00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.040
that goes out my outbox.

23
00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:09.320
So this like incredibly powerful tool and you have to review every email before

24
00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:13.600
it gets sent because that moment where it shifts to impacting, you know,

25
00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:16.120
somebody’s opinion of you outside of your own organization,

26
00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:17.840
like that's an important line that it's going to cross.

27
00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.200
A non reversible as well.

28
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:19.840
It's non-reversible.

29
00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:20.680
It's not a retaining door.

30
00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:20.800
Yeah.

31
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:24.880
If the agent had spent the day reading your diary,

32
00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:28.120
if the person it was going to send a message to was like your mother in law.

33
00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:30.880
Yeah. All right. You want to be able to express those circumstances.

34
00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:33.880
If you spent the day reading my diary, then I want to be in the loop before

35
00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:34.840
you email my mother in law.
